What is an ACF Bonding System?
An ACF Bonding System is a specialized setup used for bonding processes involving Anisotropic Conductive Film (ACF), which creates reliable electrical and mechanical connections between electronic components. This technology is critical for high-density interconnections in display manufacturing (LCD, OLED), flexible circuits, and semiconductor packaging where precision and miniaturization are essential.
These systems enable manufacturers to achieve micron-level alignment accuracy required for modern display panels and advanced semiconductor packages. The technology's ability to create durable connections in ultrathin form factors makes it indispensable for next-generation electronic applications, particularly in foldable displays and wearable devices.
